AB  - In this single case study, we explore the process of a digital new venture development by closely examining the long-term paths of one digital venture’s founder and their team spanning from the time when the entrepreneurial opportunity was shaped until the venture achieved sustainable growth. Adopting the process-based perspective of entrepreneurship, we elucidate how entrepreneurs effectively navigate this journey by combining two different behavioural logics (bricolage and engineering) while engaging with and disengaging from various stakeholders. Based on the analysis of our rich empirical evidence, collected over six years, we develop a set of propositions explaining how these two logics are interlinked in the process of a digital new venture development over time, as well as how they are applied for initial and subsequent engagement with stakeholders.  
