AB  - Municipalities need to understand, analyse, plan, and manage a complex set of aspects so as to make the society safer, cleaner, more liveable, more equitable, more resilient. Working on climate and circular goals is challenging when the methodologies to implement these goals are not agile. However, recently, the use of agile methodologies and design thinking is getting recognized in public organizations, as municipalities. In this small-scale pilot study, environmental quality in the infrastructure in the City of Trollhättan is considered as the main goal. The study aim to show how a rather radical shift in workflow can facilitate sustainable change in infrastructure design and maintenance, by relying heavily on a relatively small municipality’s self-designed, low cost, and data-driven agile process. Certain aspects found to be important are communication, stakeholders, selection of sensors, the agile process, decisions of places for sensors and data to collect, selection of sensors and visualization of data. 
